# M3.5.2 rollback fixture diagnostic — 2026-08-27

## Failure

The first positive local rollback-layout test created two byte- and
metadata-identical Git fixtures quickly enough to produce the same commit SHA.
The SHA-named destination correctly already existed, so the fixture rename was
refused before the release gate ran.

## Cause and correction

This demonstrates the intentional content-addressed path behavior, not a gate
failure. The prior-release fixture now receives an explicit tracked commit so it
has a distinct immutable SHA path. No server or live path was involved. The
complete suite must pass after this fixture-only correction.
